==English==
{{was wotd|2012|July|3}}

===Etymology===
From Dr. [[w:Pangloss|Pangloss]], a character in [[w:Voltaire|Voltaire]]’s ''[[w:Candide|Candide]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/pænˈɡlɑsiən/|/pænˈɡlɔsiən/|lang=en}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/pænˈɡlɒsɪən/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɑsiən|ɔsiən|ɒsɪən|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|Pan|gloss|i|an|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{context|pejorative|lang=en}} [[naively|Naively]] or [[unreasonably]] [[optimistic]].
#: ''Though he took a '''Panglossian''' view of the world in his youth, he became jaded as he grew older.''
# {{context|pejorative|lang=en}} Of or relating to the view that this is the best of all possible worlds.

